d here runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids April to May came in under 90% of normal in 37 of them. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 139% of normal in April to May but only 38% in November to December. So far in 2026, January to February came in at 18% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 21465 had its driest year in 1953 at 58% of normal.</p>"}
